<h1>Oneiros Privacy Policy</h1>
<p><em>Effective date: 17 November 2026</em></p>

<p>This privacy policy applies to the Oneiros: AI Dream Journal app (the "Application") for mobile devices, created by Velestra Apps (the "Service Provider", "we", "us"). It explains what information the Application collects, how it is used, who processes it, and the choices you have.</p>

<h2>1. Information we collect</h2>
<p><strong>Account information.</strong> When you sign in with Google, Apple or email, we receive your email address, a unique account ID, and, if you use Google or Apple sign-in, your display name and profile photo.</p>
<p><strong>Content you create.</strong> The dream descriptions you write or dictate, which are stored in your account.</p>
<p><strong>Content generated for you.</strong> For each dream the Application generates a title, a mood, a list of symbols with meanings, two interpretations (psychological and traditional), a short quote or fact, and an artwork image with a smaller thumbnail. These are stored in your account together with your dream.</p>
<p><strong>Usage and subscription information.</strong> The number of dream generations you have used in the current period, your preferences (such as language and favorites), and your subscription status. Payments are handled by Google Play; we do not receive your payment card details.</p>
<p><strong>Technical information.</strong> Your device's Internet Protocol address, device and operating system type, and crash and diagnostic data, collected through Firebase services to keep the Application working and to fix problems. <!-- Remove this paragraph if Analytics and Crashlytics are not enabled in your build. --></p>
<p><strong>Voice dictation (premium).</strong> If you use the microphone button, speech is converted to text by the speech recognition service built into your Android device. The Application does not record or store your audio. Depending on your device, Android's speech recognition may process audio using Google services under Google's own terms.</p>
<p>The Application does not collect precise location information and does not show advertising.</p>

<h2>2. How we use information</h2>
<ul>
  <li>To create your account and keep you signed in.</li>
  <li>To generate interpretations and artwork for your dreams and save them in your journal.</li>
  <li>To enforce usage limits and manage your subscription.</li>
  <li>To maintain, secure and improve the Application, and to diagnose crashes.</li>
  <li>To respond when you contact us.</li>
</ul>
<p>We do not sell your personal information.</p>

<h2>3. Service providers that process your data</h2>
<p>We use the following third-party providers, who process data on our behalf to run the Application:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Google Firebase</strong> (Authentication, Cloud Firestore, Cloud Storage, Cloud Functions<!-- , Analytics, Crashlytics -->): stores your account, dreams and artwork and runs our server code. Data is stored primarily in Google data centers in Europe.</li>
  <li><strong>Anthropic</strong>: the text of your dream is sent to Anthropic's AI models to produce the title, symbols and interpretations. Anthropic processes it under its own terms and privacy policy.</li>
  <li><strong>Image generation provider (currently Replicate)</strong>: a text description of a scene, generated from your dream, is sent to produce the artwork. We do not send your name, email or account ID with it.</li>
  <li><strong>Google Play and RevenueCat</strong>: process subscriptions and tell the Application whether your subscription is active.</li>
  <li><strong>Google Sign-In / Sign in with Apple</strong>: if you choose these sign-in methods.</li>
</ul>
<p>Providers may be located outside your country, including in the United States. We may also disclose information where required by law, to protect rights or safety, or to investigate fraud.</p>

<h2>4. AI-generated content</h2>
<p>Interpretations, symbol meanings and artwork are generated by artificial intelligence. They are intended for reflection and entertainment. They are not medical, psychological or professional advice and may contain mistakes. Please do not enter information about other people that you would not want processed by these providers.</p>
<p>Your dreams are private to your account. The Application has no public profiles or feeds. If you use the Share button, the link to your artwork can be opened by anyone who receives it.</p>

<h2>5. Retention and deletion</h2>
<p>We keep your account and dreams for as long as your account exists. You can delete individual dreams at any time from the dream's screen, which also removes its artwork.</p>
<p>You can delete your whole account in the Application under <strong>Settings &gt; Delete account</strong>. This permanently deletes your account, your dreams and your artwork. You can also request deletion without the Application at <a href="delete-account.html">the account deletion page</a> or by emailing us. Residual copies in backups are removed within a reasonable period. Subscription records held by Google Play may be kept as required by law.</p>

<h2>6. Your rights</h2>
<p>Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access, correct, export or delete your personal data, and to object to or restrict its processing. Contact us at the address below and we will respond within a reasonable time.</p>

<h2>7. Security</h2>
<p>We use access controls and encryption in transit, and your data is stored in your account area with rules that stop other users from reading it. No method of transmission or storage is completely secure.</p>

<h2>8. Children</h2>
<p>The Application is not intended for anyone under 16, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If you believe a child has provided us with personal information, contact us and we will delete it.</p>

<h2>9. Changes to this policy</h2>
<p>We may update this policy from time to time. We will post the new version on this page and update the effective date. Continued use of the Application after changes means you accept them.</p>

<h2>10. Contact us</h2>
<p>Velestra Apps &ndash; <a href="mailto:velestra.apps@proton.me">velestra.apps@proton.me</a></p>
